@startuml core-layers
' The layers of the core of Yeah.
'
' The same picture as the ASCII figure of the site and as the component
' architecture of `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md' §5, in the notation of components:
' the drivers submit to the run controller, the controller drives the model
' adapter, the tool registry and the policy, the scheduler runs what may
' run, everything that happened is written into one journal, and the
' projections read the journal.
'
' Every block names the files that implement it, as `file:line'.  The
' modules of `lib/' that this picture does not name are listed in the note
' at the end of this file, with the reason why they are not there.

package "drivers" as drivers {
  component "Human (M-x yeah)\nlib/yeah.el:37\nlib/yeah-compose.el:83\nlib/yeah-shell.el:78\nlib/yeah-doctor-ui.el:148\nlib/yeah-approval-ui.el:184" as human
  component "ACP clients\nlib/yeah-acp.el:401\nlib/yeah-acp-vocabulary.el:15\nlib/yeah-client.el:172\nlib/yeah-service-ui.el:441" as acp
  component "MCP clients\nlib/yeah-mcp.el:28\nlib/yeah-mcp-client.el:90\nlib/yeah-mcp-http.el:38\nlib/yeah-session-mcp.el:149\nlib/yeah-emcp.el:244" as mcp
  component "Batch\nlib/yeah-placement.el:199" as batch
  component "Wire\nlib/yeah-wire.el:23\nlib/yeah-wire-socket.el:57" as wire
}

package "core" as core {
  component "Session API / Run Controller\nlib/yeah-control.el:39\nlib/yeah-run.el:40\nlib/yeah-turn.el:60\nlib/yeah-loop.el:26\nlib/yeah-state.el:26\nlib/yeah-input.el:220\nlib/yeah-delegate.el:431\nlib/yeah-subagent.el:156\nlib/yeah-agent.el:167" as controller
  component "Model adapter\nprivate gptel\nlib/yeah-gptel.el:191\nlib/yeah-model.el:58\nlib/yeah-answer.el:33" as model_adapter
  component "Tool registry\ntyped, validated\nlib/yeah-tools.el:119\nlib/yeah-builtins.el:23\nlib/yeah-files.el:236\nlib/yeah-edit.el:257\nlib/yeah-git.el:276\nlib/yeah-process.el:333\nlib/yeah-emacs.el:186\nlib/yeah-trash.el:220\nlib/yeah-undo.el:48\nlib/yeah-untrusted.el:35\nlib/yeah-version.el:43\nlib/yeah-shell-guard.el:72\nlib/yeah-bridge.el:177\nlib/yeah-result.el:34\nlib/yeah-text.el:116" as registry
  component "Policy / approvals\nrules as data\nlib/yeah-perm.el:213\nlib/yeah-risk.el:90\nlib/yeah-approval.el:245\nlib/yeah-diff.el:64" as policy
  component "Execution scheduler\nonce-only, bounded, shared/exclusive\nlib/yeah-scheduler.el:294\nlib/yeah-runtime.el:113\nlib/yeah-life.el:86\nlib/yeah-proc.el:69" as scheduler
}

package "journal" as journal {
  component "Append-only versioned JSONL journal\nlib/yeah-session.el:167\nlib/yeah-events.el:204" as log
}

package "projections" as projections {
  component "Model context\nlib/yeah-context.el:60\nlib/yeah-compact.el:53\nlib/yeah-todo.el:128" as context
  component "Read models / UI\nlib/yeah-ui.el:649\nlib/yeah-journal.el:357\nlib/yeah-faces.el:240\nlib/yeah-session-list.el:45\nlib/yeah-org.el:94\nlib/yeah-markdown.el:52" as ui
  component "Session index / cost\nlib/yeah-sessions.el:51" as sessions
  component "Placements\nattached, service, batch\nlib/yeah-product.el:264\nlib/yeah-service.el:127" as placements
}

human --> controller : the prompt
acp --> controller : the request
mcp --> controller : the request
batch --> controller : the prompt
acp ..> wire : the requests of the protocol
mcp ..> wire : the requests of the protocol

controller --> model_adapter : the model is asked
controller --> registry : the tools are dispatched
controller --> policy : the effects are decided
model_adapter --> scheduler : the tools of the answer
registry --> scheduler : the tools that may run
policy --> scheduler : what may run
scheduler --> log : every event is written

log --> context : the context of the model
log --> ui : the view of the person
log --> sessions : the index and the cost
context --> placements : the model of the run
ui --> placements : the journal of the run
sessions --> placements : the cost of the run

note bottom
  The modules of lib/ that this picture does not name, and why:
  lib/yeah-codes.el -- experimental: disabled by default and not wired into the agent loop.
  lib/yeah-state-diagram.el -- the generator of the state diagram: a tool of the author, not a component of the harness at run time.
end note
@enduml
